[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[26A\u001b[1m### Modern Web Guidance\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mdialog\u001b[m: I used native \u001b[94m<dialog>\u001b[m elements opened via \u001b[94m.showModal()\u001b[m without redundant ARIA roles and cleared \u001b[94mdialog.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mreturnValue\u001b[m on close to prevent stale action values from leaking across opens (\"read \u001b[94mdialog.returnValue\u001b[m in a \u001b[94mclose\u001b[m\r\n  listener to learn which button was used, then reset it with \u001b[94mdialog.returnValue = ''\u001b[m\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mlight-dismiss-a-dialog\u001b[m: I added declarative \u001b[94mclosedby=\"any\"\u001b[m on modal dialogs and wired a bounding-rect pointer\r\n  coordinate fallback where \u001b[94mclosedBy\u001b[m is unsupported so clicks on dialog padding do not falsely dismiss the modal\u001b[K\r\n  (\"Use \u001b[94mclosedby=\"any\"\u001b[m to enable light-dismiss declaratively\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mprevent-page-scroll-under-modal-dialog\u001b[m: I applied \u001b[94moverscroll-behavior: contain\u001b[m to \u001b[94mdialog:modal\u001b[m and \u001b[94moverflow:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mhidden; overscroll-behavior: contain\u001b[m to \u001b[94mdialog::backdrop\u001b[m instead of mutating roo"]
[0.0, "o", "t \u001b[94mbody\u001b[m overflow, preventing layout\r\n  shift (\"Set \u001b[94moverflow: hidden\u001b[m (or \u001b[94moverflow: auto\u001b[m) on \u001b[94mdialog::backdrop\u001b[m so that it becomes a scroll container\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mresponsive-table\u001b[m: I wrapped data tables in focusable \u001b[94mrole=\"region\"\u001b[m containers with \u001b[94mcontainer-type: inline-size\u001b[m,\r\n  sticky headers, and an \u001b[94m@container (width < 680px)\u001b[m stacked layout that hides \u001b[94m<thead>\u001b[m and injects column labels via\r\n  CSS custom properties (\"MANDATORY: Hide column header from layout and screen readers\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: I declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\u001b[m, set \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: light dark\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m, and\r\n  paired \u001b[94mlight-dark()\u001b[m color tokens with a \u001b[94m@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\u001b[m fallback (\"Apply the \u001b[94mcolor-scheme\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  property to the \u001b[94mhtml\u001b[m element or the \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m pseudo-class\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode-toggle\u001b[m: I mapped \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\">\u001b[m overrides back to \u001b[9"]
[0.0, "o", "4m:root\u001b[m via \u001b[94m:has()\u001b[m and implemented a two-\r\n  state toggle that removes the \u001b[94mlocalStorage\u001b[m entry when returning to the system preference (\"Since \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m ... sets\r\n  \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: light dark\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m, updating the \u001b[94m<meta>\u001b[m alone is a \u001b[1mno-op\u001b[m — CSS wins\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mvalidate-input-after-interaction\u001b[m: I styled invalid inputs using \u001b[94m:user-invalid\u001b[m with a \u001b[94mWeakMap\u001b[m interaction fallback\r\n  and \u001b[94maria-invalid\u001b[m synchronization on \u001b[94mblur\u001b[m and \u001b[94minput\u001b[m so errors never fire prematurely before user interaction (\"Use\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94m:user-invalid\u001b[m to apply error styling only after interaction\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mfo\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[4D\u001b[?2026l"]
