[0.25, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[23A  sticky headers, and an \u001b[94m@container (width < 680px)\u001b[m stacked layout that hides \u001b[94m<thead>\u001b[m and injects column labels via\u001b[K\r\n  CSS custom properties (\"MANDATORY: Hide column header from layout and screen readers\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: I declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\u001b[m, set \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: light dark\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m, and\r\n  paired \u001b[94mlight-dark()\u001b[m color tokens with a \u001b[94m@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\u001b[m fallback (\"Apply the \u001b[94mcolor-scheme\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  property to the \u001b[94mhtml\u001b[m element or the \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m pseudo-class\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode-toggle\u001b[m: I mapped \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\">\u001b[m overrides back to \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m via \u001b[94m:has()\u001b[m and implemented a two-\r\n  state toggle that removes the \u001b[94mlocalStorage\u001b[m entry when returning to the system preference (\"Since \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m ... sets\r\n  \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: light dark\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m, updating the \u001b[94m<meta>\u001b[m alone is a \u001b[1mno-op\u001b[m — CSS wins\").\u001b"]
[0.0, "o", "[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mvalidate-input-after-interaction\u001b[m: I styled invalid inputs using \u001b[94m:user-invalid\u001b[m with a \u001b[94mWeakMap\u001b[m interaction fallback\r\n  and \u001b[94maria-invalid\u001b[m synchronization on \u001b[94mblur\u001b[m and \u001b[94minput\u001b[m so errors never fire prematurely before user interaction (\"Use\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94m:user-invalid\u001b[m to apply error styling only after interaction\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mforms\u001b[m: I placed visible \u001b[94m<label>\u001b[m and \u001b[94maria-describedby\u001b[m hints above inputs and disabled text auto-correction on part\r\n  numbers, SKUs, and search fields (\"DO turn off text correction on fields that hold identifiers rather than prose:\r\n  \u001b[94mautocorrect=\"off\"\u001b[m (plus \u001b[94mautocapitalize=\"off\"\u001b[m and \u001b[94mspellcheck=\"false\"\u001b[m)\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mhtml\u001b[m: I used \u001b[94m<search>\u001b[m for the inventory filter bar and native \u001b[94m<button>\u001b[m elements with \u001b[94maddEventListener()\u001b[m rather\r\n  than inline event handlers (\"DO use \u001b[94m<search>\u001b[m to enclose search and filtering mechanisms (eliminates the need for\r\n  \u001b[94mrole=\"sea"]
[0.0, "o", "rch\"\u001b[m)\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mcss\u001b[m: I organized styles into \u001b[94m@layer base, theme, layout, components, utilities\u001b[m, used \u001b[94m:not(:disabled)\u001b[m on button\r\n  hover states, and scoped \u001b[94mbox-sizing\u001b[m resets with \u001b[94m:where()\u001b[m instead of a universal \u001b[94m*\u001b[m selector (\"DO NOT use global\u001b[K\r\n  resets (styles on \u001b[94m*\u001b[m) as they cannot be overridden by web components or lower-priority cascade layers\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94maccessibility\u001b[m: I added a \u001b[94m.visually-hidden\u001b[m skip link targeting \u001b[94m<h1 id=\"main-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u001b[m, disambiguated\r\n  row action buttons with accessible labels, and centralized status announcements in a single \u001b[94maria-live=\"polite\"\u001b[m\r\n  region (\"If an element can receive keyboard focus, it must not be hidden via \u001b[94maria-hidden=\"true\"\u001b[m\").\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\n\u001b[C \t\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
