[0.0, "o", "tly checks \u001b[94mcomp.qty_available >= stillNeeded\u001b[m without decrementing a running\r\n\u001b[6Cavailable balance across lines. If a project (or multiple lines in the same project) references the same\r\n\u001b[6Ccomponent twice requiring 10 units each, and \u001b[94mqty_available\u001b[m is 10, both lines are marked \u001b[94min_stock\u001b[m / \u001b[94mreadyLines++\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Ceven though total demand is 20.\n\u001b[31D• \u001b[1mFix\u001b[m: Track a running map of remaining available stock per \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m while iterating BOM lines (similar to\r\n\u001b[6Chow \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk6f8e953aec49aefb;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_baseline/server.js#L487-L525\u0007POST /api/projects/:id/allocate-all\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 uses \u001b[94mavailMap\u001b[m).\r\n  3. \u001b[1mReducing \u001b[94;22mqty_required\u001b[39;1m Below \u001b[94;22mqty_allocated\u001b[39;1m Leaves Over-Allocated Stock\u001b[m\n\u001b[68D• \u001b[1mLocation\u001b[m: [\u001b[94mPUT /api/bom/:bomId\u001b[m](file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-\n\u001b[76Dexperiment/audio_inventory_baseline/ser\r\n\n⣻  \u001b[90mWor\u001b[94mking.\u001b[90m..\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───"]
