[0.0, "o", "[K\r\n\n\u001b[1mRun this command?\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, run command\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with 'npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest search\r\n\"responsive data table\"'\u001b[K\r\n  3. Yes, and always allow for commands that start with 'npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest search \"responsive data\u001b[K\r\ntable\"' (Persist to settings.json)\r\n  4. No, cancel\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mctrl+g\u001b[90;22m edit/expand command\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[3.471, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[30A\t\u001b[1mFix\u001b[m: Wrap API calls (or catch inside \u001b[94mapi()\u001b[m) to call \u001b[94mannounceStatus(err.message)\u001b[m on failure.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### 3. Performance & Code Quality Opportunities\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n  • **N+1 Queries in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8eb341cf1f90abc2;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_baseline/db.js#L441-L503\u0007getAllProjects\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf3a45d3d631eff30;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_baseline/db.js#L587-L679\u0007getShoppingList\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007**:\r\n      • Both functions query \u001b[94mSELECT * FROM bom_items WHERE project_id = ?\u001b[m inside a loop over all projects. Fetching\r\n      all relevant \u001b[94mbom_items\u001b[m in a single query and grouping by \u001b[94mproject_id\u001b[m in memory (or via SQL \u001b[94mJOIN\u001b[m) will avoid\r\n\u001b[6Crepeated prepared statement creation and execution on every \u001b[94m/api/overview\u001b[m load.\r\n  • \u001b[1mCSV Parser Line Splitting on Quoted Newlines\u001b[m:\u001b[K\n\u001b[44D\u001b[1K • \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2bf0e9ad5c"]
[0.0, "o", "af323c;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_baseline/public/app.js#L870-L922\u0007parseCsvText\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 splits on \u001b[94m/\\r?\\n/\u001b[m before parsing quotes, which will break if a CSV cell contains a multiline\r\n\u001b[6Cnote inside quotes.\r\n  • \u001b[1mCSS Mobile Table First-Column Alignment\u001b[m:\u001b[K\n\u001b[39D\u001b[1K • In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk1aea8624d7e1ba86;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_baseline/public/styles.css#L700-L740\u0007styles.css:700-740\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94m#bom-table\u001b[m has a checkbox in the first column (\u001b[94mtd:nth-child(1)\u001b[m) and \u001b[94m<th scope=\"row\">\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cin the second column (\u001b[94mnth-child(2)\u001b[m), whereas \u001b[94m#components-table\u001b[m and \u001b[94m#shopping-table\u001b[m have \u001b[94m<th scope=\"row\">\u001b[m in the\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K first column (\u001b[94mnth-child(1)\u001b[m). As a result, in the \u001b[94m< 680px\u001b[m container view on \u001b[94m#bom-table\u001b[m, \u001b[94mtd:nth-child(2)::before\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K doesn't match the \u001b[94m<th scope=\"row\">\u001b[m designator cell, shifting the mobile labels by one column"]
